-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 — the seat layer.
--
-- SEAT: the accused person — the individual whose acts are measured against
-- an offence and who may be charged and punished under it.
--
-- This layer phrases the existing rules of this encoding as the questions the
-- accused person would ask ("Have I committed theft", "What can I be made to
-- suffer under section 409"). Every question below takes the same facts
-- record as the rule it wraps and calls that rule; none of the rules, facts
-- records or charge builders in the other modules is changed, and no new law
-- is added here.
--
-- Where the existing encoding departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18,
-- it is recorded here and not fixed:
--   * it was written from the prosecutor's seat: its outputs are charges in
--     the form the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 ss 123-126 prescribe, with
--     refusals under CPC s 123(5); that charge machinery is from another Act;
--   * the states of mind the court finds (intention, knowledge, dishonest or
--     fraudulent intent, good faith) are taken as facts the record states,
--     not answered conditionally ("..., if the court finds that ...");
--   * the scope is a selection of offences (ss 22-25, 301, 321, 323A,
--     378-380, 383-384, 390-394, 403, 405-409, 415, 417, 420, 503, 506), not
--     every operative section of the Code.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `penal-code-general`
IMPORT `theft-378-379`
IMPORT `misappropriation-403`
IMPORT `cbt-405-406`
IMPORT `cbt-407-409`
IMPORT `cheating-415-417-420`
IMPORT `extortion-383-384`
IMPORT `robbery-390-392`
IMPORT `criminal-intimidation-503-506`
IMPORT `hurt-321-323A`
IMPORT `culpable-homicide-301`
IMPORT `charge-sheet`

§ `When I am said to have taken or kept someone else's property`

-- s 378. "Theft": intending to take movable property dishonestly out of
-- another person's possession without consent, moving it in order to take it.
GIVEN f IS A `Theft Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed theft` f IF
    `commits theft` f

-- s 379. The punishment for theft, as the charge under s 379 recites it.
GIVEN f IS A `Theft Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`What can I be made to suffer for theft under section 379` f MEANS
    (`charge under s 379` f)'s punishment

-- s 380. Theft "in dwelling": theft in a building, tent or vessel used as a
-- human dwelling or for the custody of property.
GIVEN f IS A `Theft in Dwelling Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished for theft in a dwelling under section 380` f IF
    `offence under s 380` f

-- s 403. "Dishonest misappropriation": dishonestly taking for my own use, or
-- converting, movable property that is not mine (for example, property I
-- found or took by mistake).
GIVEN f IS A `Misappropriation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I dishonestly misappropriated property` f IF
    `offence under s 403` f

§ `When property was entrusted to me`

-- s 405. "Criminal breach of trust": being entrusted with property, or with
-- dominion over it, and dishonestly misappropriating, converting, using or
-- disposing of it in violation of the trust, or suffering another to do so.
GIVEN f IS A `CBT Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed criminal breach of trust` f IF
    `commits criminal breach of trust` f

-- s 408. Criminal breach of trust by a clerk or servant: the property was
-- entrusted to me in my capacity as an employee.
GIVEN c IS AN `Aggravated CBT Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished under section 408 as an employee` c IF
    `offence under s 408` c

-- s 409. Criminal breach of trust by a public servant, a director or key
-- executive, or someone entrusted in the way of a trade, profession or
-- business as a banker, merchant, factor, broker, attorney or agent: the
-- punishment, as the charge under s 409 recites it.
GIVEN c IS AN `Aggravated CBT Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`What can I be made to suffer under section 409` c MEANS
    (`charge under s 409` c)'s punishment

§ `When I am said to have deceived or threatened someone`

-- s 415. "Cheating": deceiving a person and, fraudulently or dishonestly,
-- inducing them to deliver property, consent to its retention, or do or
-- omit something they would not otherwise do.
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I cheated` f IF
    cheats f

-- s 420. Cheating that dishonestly induces delivery of property. A charge
-- "can be framed" when the facts fulfil every legal condition of the offence
-- (CPC s 123(5)).
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be charged under section 420` f IF
    (`charge under s 420` f)'s `made out`

-- s 383. "Extortion": intentionally putting a person in fear of injury and
-- so dishonestly inducing them to deliver property.
GIVEN f IS AN `Extortion Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed extortion` f IF
    `commits extortion` f

-- s 390. "Robbery": theft or extortion aggravated by causing, attempting or
-- putting in fear of instant death, hurt or wrongful restraint.
GIVEN f IS A `Robbery Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed robbery` f IF
    `commits robbery` f

-- s 393. Attempting to commit robbery.
GIVEN f IS A `Robbery Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished for attempted robbery under section 393` f IF
    `offence under s 393` f

-- s 394. Voluntarily causing hurt in committing or attempting robbery, and
-- the joint liability of anyone jointly concerned.
GIVEN f IS A `Robbery Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished for hurt caused in a robbery under section 394` f IF
    `offence under s 394` f

-- s 503. "Criminal intimidation": threatening injury to a person, their
-- reputation or property, with intent to cause alarm or to make them do or
-- omit something.
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed criminal intimidation` f IF
    `commits criminal intimidation` f

-- s 506. The heavier limb: a threat to cause death or grievous hurt, or
-- destruction of property by fire, or the other injuries the limb lists.
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the heavier punishment under section 506 apply to me` f IF
    `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` f

§ `When someone was hurt or killed`

-- s 321. "Voluntarily causes hurt": doing an act intending to cause hurt, or
-- knowing it likely, and thereby causing hurt.
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I voluntarily caused hurt` f IF
    `voluntarily causes hurt` f

-- s 323A. Voluntarily causing hurt which causes "grievous hurt" (the serious
-- hurts listed in s 320) when the hurt intended or known likely was not
-- grievous.
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished under section 323A for grievous hurt I did not intend` f IF
    `offence under s 323A` f

-- s 301(1). Transferred malice: where I meant, or knew I was likely, to kill
-- one person and caused the death of another, the culpable homicide takes
-- the description it would have had if I had killed the person I intended.
GIVEN k IS A Killing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the death I caused judged by what I intended for someone else` k IF
    `the circumstances mentioned in subsection (1)` k

-- s 301(2). A defence or exception in law that would have been open to me
-- had I killed the person I intended is open to me for the death I caused.
GIVEN k IS A Killing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a defence or exception in law available to me` k IF
    `a defence or exception in law is available to the accused person` k

§ `What I can be charged with`

-- The punishing sections under which a charge can be framed against me on
-- the facts of one complaint, most serious first within each family.
GIVEN c IS A Complaint
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`What can I be charged with` c MEANS
    `applicable charges` c
